TITLE:Rec Dec Traditions
H1:Rec dec traditions: seven approved, eight to pick from <span class="draft">pitch v2 · plan only</span>
SUB:The user (2026-10-19): when the rec dec is switched on (after Pillar 5's Steps 3 and 4), it comes with about a dozen traditions of its own. v1 pitched twelve; the user kept seven and dropped five. v2 shows the seven as approved (with Glow paddle earlier and a rota for Wren talks), and pitches eight new candidates for the five remaining places, with my top five marked. Written by the Pillar 5 designer for lead 16. No game code.
NAV:v2=What changed|week=The week|ok=The seven approved|pick=Eight to pick from|fit=How they fit|q=Questions

<section id="v2">
  <h2>What changed in v2</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Approved</b> (the user, ~02:30): the Lightdisc Cup, Dawn swim, Wall night, Paddle club, Float hour, Wren talks, Glow paddle.</li>
    <li><b>Glow paddle comes earlier:</b> first on <b>Day 27</b> (the Saturday after Calder's question, the first quiet Saturday evening after the arc), and every four weeks from then (Days 27, 55, 83 ...) instead of once a season.</li>
    <li><b>Wren talks, "do other talks too":</b> a rota of six speakers from six departments (below); about every two weeks after the first.</li>
    <li><b>Dropped:</b> Rookie court, Open stage, Lanes night, Zero-G games, Season splash.</li>
    <li><b>New:</b> eight candidates for the five places left. My top five are marked ★.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="week">
  <h2>The week</h2>
  <p class="note"><span class="tag new">gold</span> approved rec dec tradition · <span class="tag">teal</span> rec dec tradition already planned · <span class="tag old">grey</span> candidate (★ my pick) · plain text: the ship's other traditions. "2-wk" and "4-wk" run every two or four weeks.</p>
  <div class="week">
    <div class="day"><h4>Monday</h4><p>Gym club · Lap of the Wren · Sunrise stretch · Book circle (2-wk) · Department cup (4-wk) · the Captain's all-hands (first Monday of a season)</p><p><span class="tag new">Wren talks 20:00 (about 2-wk)</span></p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Tuesday</h4><p>Knit and natter · Spice shelf supper · Tiles night · Open lab (4-wk) · Bridge hour (4-wk)</p><p><span class="tag new">Dawn swim 06:15</span> <span class="tag new">Wall night 18:30</span></p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Wednesday</h4><p>Pick-your-own breakfast · Sunrise stretch · Brennan's tasting table · Open door · Late piano</p><p><span class="tag new">Paddle club 18:30</span> <span class="tag new">Float hour 21:30</span></p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Thursday</h4><p>Postcard night · Late piano · Quiz night 20:00</p><p><span class="tag new">Dawn swim 06:15</span> <span class="tag old">★ Kit mend night 18:00 (4-wk)</span></p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Friday</h4><p>Sunrise stretch · Works Friday tea · Music jam · Tap night</p><p><span class="tag old">★ Junior night 19:00 (2-wk)</span> <span class="tag old">★ Sing-along 21:00</span></p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Saturday</h4><p>Long breakfast · Garden hour · Cook-along · Tiles ladder · Harvest morning (2-wk) · Sowing morning (season) · Observatory night</p><p><span class="tag">Film night 20:00</span> <span class="tag old">Captain's lengths 07:00 (4-wk)</span> <span class="tag new">Glow paddle 22:30 (4-wk)</span></p></div>
    <div class="day"><h4>Sunday</h4><p>Sunday swap meet · Sunday long table · Reading corner</p><p><span class="tag old">Slow stretch 08:30</span> <span class="tag">Regatta / Ring the bell 09:30 (4-wk)</span> <span class="tag">Winner Stays On 11:30</span> <span class="tag new">Lightdisc Cup 11:30 (4-wk, in its place)</span> <span class="tag old">★ Night-shift matinee 15:00</span> <span class="tag old">Beach stories 16:00 (4-wk)</span> <span class="tag">Talent night 19:30 (4-wk)</span></p></div>
  </div>
  <p class="note">Plus <span class="tag old">★ Birthday bell</span>: on any crew birthday, 18:30 at the climbing wall. No two rec dec traditions share a room at once; the evening ones end before quiz night, and each draws 6-12 people, inside the rec dec's evening cap of about 15 (the Cup and Junior night are gatherings, exempt like talent night).</p>
</section>

<section id="ok">
  <h2>The seven approved</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Tradition</th><th>When · where</th><th>Who</th><th>What you do</th><th>You get</th><th>First</th></tr>
    <tr><td><b>The Lightdisc Cup</b></td><td>Every four weeks, Sunday 11:30-16:30 (between a regatta and Ring the bell) · court and stands</td><td>Pell runs the bracket; pairs from each department; full stands (a gathering)</td><td>Enter with a partner (tap Pell, pick a friend) and play your matches in the Lightdisc game, or cheer.</td><td>leisure and social; a friendship step with your partner; department reputation if you go far; names on the foyer's Cup board</td><td>Day 28; takes Winner Stays On's slot that Sunday</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Dawn swim</b></td><td>Tuesdays and Thursdays 06:15-06:45 · the pool</td><td>Rina, before the infirmary opens</td><td>Tap a lane: the swimming animation under the hull windows.</td><td>hygiene and energy; a friendship step with Rina over a few weeks</td><td>Day 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Wall night</b></td><td>Tuesdays 18:30-19:45 · the climbing wall</td><td>Tomas belays</td><td>Tap the wall to climb; ring the bell at the top.</td><td>leisure; a friendship step with Tomas; your name on the season's bell board</td><td>Day 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Paddle club</b></td><td>Wednesdays 18:30-19:30 · the river hall</td><td>Chief Holt</td><td>Tap the kayak dock: the slow loop, then the fast run once Holt says you're ready (after three visits).</td><td>leisure; Holt warms to you</td><td>Day 3</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Float hour</b></td><td>Wednesdays 21:30-22:15 · the float room</td><td>Matthias Oduya dims the orbs; quiet music; no talking</td><td>Tap to float.</td><td>rest and mood (a calmer night's sleep)</td><td>Day 3</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Wren talks</b></td><td>About every two weeks, Monday 20:00-20:45 · the auditorium</td><td>A speaker from a different department each time (the rota below); Commander Vance chairs</td><td>Listen (a short meeting panel) and ask one question if you like. Later you can be asked to give one.</td><td>a little social, a "learned" note in the Ship app; a friendship step with the speaker if you ask</td><td>Day 8</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Glow paddle</b> <span class="note">(earlier, v2)</span></td><td>Every four weeks, Saturday 22:30-23:30 (after film night) · the river hall, lights off</td><td>Holt leads; kayaks with little lanterns on the slow loop, stars through the port windows</td><td>Tap the dock to paddle with a lantern, or watch from the pebble beach.</td><td>mood and social; a quiet friendship step with whoever paddles beside you</td><td><b>Day 27</b> (then 55, 83 ...)</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <h3>The Wren talks rota (the first six)</h3>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Day</th><th>Speaker</th><th>Department</th><th>The talk</th></tr>
    <tr><td>8 Mon</td><td>Dr. Imra Sato</td><td>Survey</td><td>"What lives between the stars": the creature that swam off at dinner that evening</td></tr>
    <tr><td>29 Mon</td><td>Zeke Torres</td><td>Works (engine)</td><td>"How a drive coil sings": why the engine room hums in three notes</td></tr>
    <tr><td>43 Mon</td><td>Chef Auda Brennan</td><td>Galley</td><td>"A spice for every port": the spice shelf, jar by jar (with tasting)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>57 Mon</td><td>Comms Chief Lucia Ferreira</td><td>Comms</td><td>"Messages that came home late": the longest a letter has taken to reach the Wren</td></tr>
    <tr><td>71 Mon</td><td>Rina and Dr. Nandakumar</td><td>Infirmary</td><td>"What the Wren cough taught us" (after the cough, Days 50-53)</td></tr>
    <tr><td>85 Mon</td><td>Chief Bram Holt</td><td>Watch</td><td>"The oldest log in the Watch office": the night the Wren's first crew nearly lost the lift</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <p class="note">Then Chief Calder ("The Wren's first refit"), Yara Esposito ("Where every crate goes"), Envoy Saruth (a Veyli talk, if you know them well), and you, once you're an Engine Specialist ("What I learned in my first month"). Day 8 is the only Monday inside the career arc that isn't a career day (1, 15 and 22 are), so the rota starts again after the arc.</p>
</section>

<section id="pick">
  <h2>Eight to pick from (five places)</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Candidate</th><th>When · where</th><th>Who</th><th>What you do</th><th>You get</th><th>First</th></tr>
    <tr><td><b>★ Junior night</b><br><span class="note">social · your peers</span></td><td>Every two weeks, Friday 19:00-21:00 · the whole rec dec</td><td>The juniors take over the deck: Tomas, Pell and Rina organise, the bunkmates come (a gathering)</td><td>Tap anything: the court, the pool, the kayaks, the float room; hang about with the bunk rooms.</td><td>lots of social; friendship steps with your bunkmates; it still counts as yours after you're promoted ("once a junior")</td><td>Day 12</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>★ Birthday bell</b><br><span class="note">social · ties to birthdays</span></td><td>On every crew birthday, 18:30-18:45 · the climbing wall</td><td>The birthday person climbs and rings the bell; their friends cheer; then the cake at 20:15 as now</td><td>Cheer (be there), or belay for a friend (tap them). On your own birthday, you ring it.</td><td>social; a friendship step with the birthday person if you're there</td><td>the first crew birthday after Day 1</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>★ Sing-along</b><br><span class="note">creative · music</span></td><td>Fridays 21:00-22:00 · the auditorium (after the jam)</td><td>Lucia Ferreira leads; Maeve Volkov on the lights; songs from everyone's home</td><td>Sing along (be there), or pick a song to lead (the talent night act picker: three songs from home).</td><td>social and mood; a friendship step with Lucia; your song becomes "yours" in chatter</td><td>Day 5 (the evening the storm ends)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>★ Kit mend night</b><br><span class="note">Works · cozy</span></td><td>Every four weeks, Thursday 18:00-19:30 · the kit hire desk</td><td>Maeve Volkov (who keeps the rec dec's machines) and whoever wants to help</td><td>Fix rec kit: split paddles, torn disc gloves, a stiff harness (short Tier 1 work steps at the desk, no board jobs).</td><td>reputation with Works and the rec crowd; Maeve's friendship; your initials on a paddle</td><td>Day 18</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>★ Night-shift matinee</b><br><span class="note">kind · quiet</span></td><td>Sundays 15:00-17:00 · the auditorium</td><td>Maeve runs the projector; the night shift, who sleep through Saturday's film night, and anyone else</td><td>Take a seat: Saturday's film again, for the people who missed it.</td><td>leisure; friendship with the night-shift crew (who you'll work beside on Days 19-20)</td><td>Day 7</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Captain's lengths</b><br><span class="note">rare · a quiet moment</span></td><td>Every four weeks, Saturday 07:00-07:30 · the pool</td><td>Captain Marrow swims lengths; anyone may take the next lane</td><td>Tap the next lane: a few lengths beside the Captain, then a line or two from her.</td><td>hygiene; a little friendship with the Captain (a rare chance)</td><td>Day 27 (with Glow paddle that night: a rec dec Saturday)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Beach stories</b><br><span class="note">quiet · stories</span></td><td>Every four weeks, Sunday 16:00-16:45 · the river hall's pebble beach</td><td>Someone reads aloud: Envoy Saruth's Veyli tales first, then crew from home</td><td>Sit on the beach and listen.</td><td>mood and a little social</td><td>Day 14 (with the Veyli guests aboard)</td></tr>
    <tr><td><b>Slow stretch</b><br><span class="note">active · gentle</span></td><td>Sundays 08:30-09:15 · the float room</td><td>Dr. Nandakumar leads a stretch at a fifth of gravity</td><td>Tap to join: the float animation, slower.</td><td>energy and mood for the day</td><td>Day 7</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <p class="note">Why these five: Junior night and the Birthday bell are about people you already know; Sing-along and Kit mend night add music and Works (the rec dec had neither); the matinee gives the night shift something, before your own night shift. Captain's lengths is the close sixth.</p>
</section>

<section id="fit">
  <h2>How they fit (traditions, events, career)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>What they move or replace:</b> the Cup takes Winner Stays On's slot one Sunday in four. Nothing else moves.</li>
    <li><b>The events plan (approved v4):</b> the storm (Days 4-5) pauses Thursday's traditions after 14:00, and its all-clear (Friday 18:30) comes before Day 5's Sing-along. Day 8's creature leaves at 18:40, before Sato's talk about it. Day 14's Beach stories has the Veyli aboard. Day 18's Kit mend night ends before Echo Signal (20:30). Day 21's distress call (11:30-16:30) pauses that Sunday's afternoon traditions. Day 24's Loss of Power is a morning. Day 27's Glow paddle and Captain's lengths have no event near them.</li>
    <li><b>The career's big days:</b> nothing is aimed at you on Days 9-11, 15-16, 22-23 or 26; the Monday rota skips them. Day 12's Junior night is your first Friday as an Officer.</li>
    <li><b>Buildable with what exists:</b> the tradition engine's rhythms (weekly, two-weekly, four-weekly, birthdays), tap-to-join, gatherings, the rec dec's planned animations and Lightdisc game, the talent night act picker, the meeting panel and work steps. New: the Cup's bracket, the boards' names, a speaker rota table, and kit mend's three small work steps.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="q">
  <h2>Questions for the user (with my recommendations)</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><b>Which five of the eight?</b> <i>Recommended: the five marked ★ (Junior night, Birthday bell, Sing-along, Kit mend night, Night-shift matinee).</i></li>
    <li><b>Glow paddle every four weeks from Day 27</b>, or more often? <i>Recommended: every four weeks, so it stays special.</i></li>
    <li><b>Wren talks every two weeks after the arc</b>, with a speaker from a different department each time? <i>Recommended: yes.</i></li>
    <li><b>Do you play your Cup matches yourself</b> (the live Lightdisc game)? <i>Recommended: yes; the other pairs' results are seeded.</i></li>
    <li><b>Can you give a Wren talk later</b> (as an Engine Specialist)? <i>Recommended: yes, once, after the arc.</i></li>
  </ol>
</section>
